# Rubix Lab host list - copy to hosts.txt and fill in your real addresses.
#
# One machine per line:   <ip or hostname>  [role]
# Blank lines and anything after # are ignored. Every controller tool reads
# this file through fleet.py.
#
# hosts.txt only records two kinds of FIXED, DURABLE facts about a machine:
#
#   1. A fixed role - a permanent identity for that machine:
#        fullnode       one node at port 20000, run with -fullnode, no DID.
#                       List every fullnode; the first one is the bootstrap
#                       seed and is installed first, with an empty list.
#        faucet         one node at port 20000 holding the faucet DID
#        faucet-quorum  one node at port 20000 holding the faucet quorum DID
#        explorer       the explorer - runs no node
#        controller     this machine - runs no node
#      Leave the role column blank for every other machine: it is a POOL
#      machine and runs every node in systems/node-layout.txt (9 nodes, with
#      the DID count each node holds).
#
#   2. Unavailable - comment the line out with a reason + date, so every tool
#      skips it automatically, without losing the record of why:
#        # 10.0.0.20  # down - unreachable since 2026-08-18
#
# Do NOT write "quorum", "sender" or "receiver" here. Those are per-test-case
# assignments made at test-execution time from the pool nodes - not a fixed
# property of a machine, since which nodes act as quorum changes every cycle.

10.0.0.11  fullnode
10.0.0.12  fullnode
10.0.0.13  faucet
10.0.0.14  faucet-quorum
10.0.0.15  controller
10.0.0.16  explorer
10.0.0.20
10.0.0.21
10.0.0.22
